  "description": "Demolition of existing residential building and redevlopment social houseing comprising 10 No 1 bed flats and 2 No 2 bed flats with associated car parking and external works.",
  "site_name": "St Lawrence Business Centre",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "02/02/2000",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW13 7LT",
  "street_name": "Victoria Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major traveller caravan pitches",
  "lapsed_date": "03/02/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 7am to 6pm on Mondays to Friday and 8am to 1pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 4 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\n(iv)\tmeasures to minimise noise and general disturbance during construction works for adjoining residential and school users.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The windows formed in the north western elevation of the building shall be obscure glazed and shall not be replaced or repaired otherwise than with obscured glazing.",
    "Condition : 6 - The scheme of sound insulation detailed in Bickerdike Allen Partners reports dated 21/1/2000 and 6/6/2000 shall be carried out before any part of the development hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 7 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority and these works shall be carried out as approved.  These details shall include (proposed finished levels or contours; means of enclosure; car parking layouts; other vehicle and pedestrian access and circulation areas; hard surfacing material; minor artefacts and structures (eg. furniture, play equipment, refuse or other storage units, signs, lighting etc); proposed and existing functional services above and below ground (eg drainage power, communications cables, pipelines etc. indicating lines, manholes, supports etc); retained historic landscape features and proposals for restoration, where relevant).\r\n\r\nSoft landscape works shall include (planting plans; written specifications (including cultivation and other operations associated with plant and grass establishment); schedules of plants, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers/densities where appropriate; implementation programme)\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - No development shall take place until a schedule of landscape maintenance for a minimum period of 5 years has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  The schedule shall include details of the arrangements for its implementation.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved schedule",
    "Condition : 9 - Before commencement of any operations on site full details of the tree protection measures to be taken shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority, and the measures shall be carried out as approved.",
    "Condition : 10 - Surface water drainage works shall be carried out in accordance with details which shall have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before development commences."
  ],
